2. Who may use Premium Material

A purchase or an explicit written gift or evaluation grant from the Licensor
must authorize your access. The order or grant identifies one named user
unless the Licensor expressly grants additional seats. A coupon alone,
repository access, a download link, or the absence of technical activation
does not grant a license to Premium Material.

Subject to this license and the applicable order or written grant, the
Licensor grants the authorized user a non-exclusive, non-transferable right
to use the delivered Premium Material for personal work, internal business
work, and commercial or client projects.

3. Permitted use

The authorized user may:

- Install and use the kit on their own or employer-managed devices, and
  across multiple projects, for that user's work.
- Make private modifications and reasonable backup copies.
- Use chosen coding-agent services to process the material solely to assist
  that user's authorized work, subject to those services' terms. This does
  not permit publishing it as a shared skill, dataset, or hosted kit service.
- Create, sell, license, publish, and deliver their own project output.
  This includes application code, task records, and project-specific
  configuration and managed instruction blocks generated using the kit.

The Licensor claims no ownership of your original project output merely
because you used the kit. This output permission does not authorize
redistribution of the Premium skill library, reusable CLI source, or
Premium documentation as a substitute for the kit. Open-source components
within any output keep their own applicable license requirements.

